  "name": "IMMUNOFIXATION ELECTROPHORESIS (MM , SERUM)",
  "code": "2843",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Immunotyping is not a quantitative assay. If a monoclonal protein is identified, a serum protein<br>electrophoresis assay is required for quantifying the abnormality.</p>\n<p><strong>Comment</strong><br>The assay is used for immunotyping of monoclonal proteins which identifies the monoclonal immunoglobulin<br>heavy-chain (gamma, alpha, mu) and/or light-chain type (kappa or lambda). It is generally recommended that<br>both serum Protein electrophoresis (SPEP) and Immunotyping be used as a screening panel because it is more<br>sensitive than SPEP. Immunotyping is not only recommended as part of the initial screening process but also for<br>confirmation of complete response to therapy.</p>\n<p><strong>Usage</strong><br>Identification of monoclonal immunoglobulin heavy and light chains documentation of complete response to&nbsp;therapy.</p>",
  "showInterpretation": false,
  "sampleType": "serum",
